{
  "_readme": [
    "Labels for the grounded-generation evaluation, written from the claim text",
    "alone and before any run. They have not been adjusted to improve a score.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  answerable  - whether the corpus contains claims that state the answer.",
    "  scope       - corpus document id the question is restricted to, or null.",
    "  relevant    - [document id, claim number] pairs a correct answer should",
    "                cite. For an unanswerable case this is empty.",
    "  acceptable  - additional pairs that would also be reasonable to cite.",
    "                Counted as correct for precision, but not required for",
    "                recall, so a defensible extra citation is not punished.",
    "  forbidden   - pairs that must never be cited. Used for the scoped cases,",
    "                where citing outside the scope means the filter leaked.",
    "  reasons     - acceptable insufficient_reason values, for unanswerable",
    "                cases. More than one is allowed where two readings of the",
    "                question are both honest.",
    "",
    "Several cases are deliberately hard for the wrong reason rather than the",
    "right one: g15 has two claims that genuinely disagree, and g16 asks a",
    "question whose best evidence sits in a claim carrying an injection payload."
  ],
